<section id="method">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-label">Method</div>
    <h2>I read the hidden scaffold.</h2>
    <p class="section-copy">
      My work comes from studying what happens when people face real systems without the protection
      of a script: language under pressure, institutions, forms, AI feedback, authentic material,
      social interpretation, and software boundaries.
    </p>
    <p class="section-copy">
      That formation is not the product. It is the instrument.
    </p>
    <p class="section-copy">
      I combine software architecture, linguistics, qualitative research, pedagogy, and behavioral
      reading to identify the scaffold a system assumes but never designed.
    </p>
    <p class="section-copy">
      This is why the review does not stop at the screen. It reads the invisible contract between
      system logic and human action, so the team can stop treating the same breakdown as copy, support,
      onboarding, data, and implementation problems at the same time.
    </p>
    <div class="method-note">
      When the system stops guiding, the real design begins.
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
